---
interface Props {
  compact?: boolean;
}
const { compact = false } = Astro.props;
---

<section id="capacity-basis" class={compact ? 'border-y border-steel-200 bg-steel-50 py-8' : 'section bg-steel-50'}>
  <div class="container-x">
    <div class="max-w-3xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Capacity basis</p>
      <h2 class="mt-2 font-display text-2xl font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-steel-900 sm:text-3xl">
        Compare capacity on the same basis
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-steel-700">
        A capacity figure is only meaningful when the basis is stated. Before comparing two models or
        two suppliers, confirm whether the number refers to wheat intake or finished flour output, the
        operating hours per day, the extraction rate, the wheat specification and the test conditions.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[720px] border-collapse text-left text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-steel-300">
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold text-steel-900">Parameter</th>
            <th class="py-3 pr-4 font-semibold text-steel-900">What to confirm</th>
            <th class="py-3 font-semibold text-steel-900">Why it changes the comparison</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody class="text-steel-700">
          <tr class="border-b border-steel-200">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium text-steel-900">Capacity basis</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Wheat input or finished flour output</td>
            <td class="py-3">The same mill has different t/d figures under the two definitions.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-steel-200">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium text-steel-900">Operating time</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">24-hour continuous or actual shift pattern</td>
            <td class="py-3">A 10-hour shift is not comparable with a 24-hour rating.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-steel-200">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium text-steel-900">Extraction rate</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Flour yield from wheat, by product mix</td>
            <td class="py-3">Higher extraction changes flour output and power per tonne.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-steel-200">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium text-steel-900">Wheat condition</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Moisture, hardness, variety and cleanliness</td>
            <td class="py-3">Difficult wheat reduces throughput and changes conditioning.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr class="border-b border-steel-200">
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium text-steel-900">Power</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Installed power or measured consumption</td>
            <td class="py-3">Installed kW is not the same as kWh per tonne.</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4 font-medium text-steel-900">Scope</td>
            <td class="py-3 pr-4">Cleaning, milling, sifting, packing and civil works</td>
            <td class="py-3">Capacity outside the quoted scope is not comparable.</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-steel-600">
      Haiyun quotes a plant against an agreed wheat specification, flow sheet and operating pattern.
      Catalogue tables are a selection guide, not a performance guarantee; the quotation and approved
      flow sheet define the contractual basis.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
